  bl.1 pickup ignition key||The pickup no longer starts; the key provides a reason to promise he is going home.
  bl.2 cedar boat||A new unfinished carving meant to replace the one Elmer kept for decades.
  bl.3 folded newspaper|Base.Newspaper|Protects tables from shavings; Otis reads sale notices long after the sales ceased.
  bl.4 stub pencil|Base.Pencil|Marks machinery measurements and names he does not want to lose.
  bl.5 patched overalls||Ada's old patch is beneath three newer repairs near the pocket.
  bl.6 Raymond's envelope||An empty envelope addressed in Raymond's careful lettering, kept flat behind the newspaper.
  rl.1 Elmer Voss|lifelong friend|First-grade companion; alive when last seen at his gate, keeps a blue cup for Otis.
  rl.2 Raymond Pell|former companion|Army clerk whose careful letters Otis saved; sent away after a three-day visit in 1968.
  rl.3 Ada Wright|mother, died 1962|Made him remove muddy overalls before supper and corrected his inflated accounts.
end

