  bl.1 wedding band||Ruth had it resized twice; turning it gives him time to avoid an answer.
  bl.2 small notebook|Base.Notebook|Contains dates of Reserve renewals, plant shifts and pension payments.
  bl.3 pencil|Base.Pencil|Sharpened carefully so his small writing remains legible.
  bl.4 unfinished clothespin||A carving made to Ruth's preferred width although she can no longer test it.
  bl.5 field jacket||An old repaired jacket with his pension cash concealed inside a patch.
  bl.6 prescription bottle||Carries his own diabetes medication; kept out of sight when asking for ordinary help.
  rl.1 Ruth Sanders|wife, died 1986|Dressmaker who tested his carved clothespins and resized his ring.
  rl.2 Nina Vaught|adult daughter|Born 1956; moved to Cincinnati in 1978 after Lowell opposed her marriage.
  rl.3 Jean Mercer|sister|Last relative seen before leaving; asked him to visit Nina and received an unkept promise.
end

